 ],
 "literal": "Those who performed penance surely, O friend, coolly / drizzling droplets in the cold severe month, / pasture grass having grazed, with the majestic bull, / ground-hanging dewlap, swollen-uddered cows, / milk dripping, thinking of their calves, leaving the herd, / towards the village returning in the sorrowful evening, / having gone bound by the pursuit of hard-to-obtain wealth, / the return of their separated-living lovers, those who see!",
 "translation": "O friend, surely those women must have performed great penance! In this cold, severe month when cool droplets drizzle, during this sorrowful evening when the cows—with dewlaps hanging to the ground and udders swollen with dripping milk—having grazed on pasture grass with the majestic bull, think of their calves, leave the herd, and return to the village, they are able to see the return of their lovers who had gone away, bound by the pursuit of hard-to-obtain wealth.",
 "modern": "தோழியே! குளிர்ந்த துளிகள் தூவுகின்ற பனிக்காலத்துக் கடுமையான இத்திங்களில், புல்வெளியில் மேய்ந்துவிட்டு, பெருமையுடைய காளையோடு, நிலத்தில் அசையும் தாடையையும் பால் சுரந்து வீங்கிய மடியையும் உடைய பசுக்கள், தம் கன்றுகளை நினைத்துப் பாலைச் சொரிந்தவாறே மந்தையை விட்டு நீங்கி ஊரை நோக்கித் திரும்புகின்ற இந்தத் துன்பம் தரும் மாலைப் பொழுதில், பெறுவதற்கரிய பொருளைத் தேடிச் சென்று பிரிந்து வாழும் காதலர் திரும்பி வருவதைக் காண்கின்றாரே, அவர்கள் நிச்சயமாகத் தவம் செய்தவர்கள் ஆவர்.",
 "explanation": "In this poem, the heroine is speaking to her friend during the cold season when her lover is away on a quest for wealth. She observes the evening scene where the cows, accompanied by a majestic bull, return to the village with udders swollen with milk, eager to reunite with their calves. This sight of domestic reunion intensifies her own feelings of loneliness and longing. She remarks that only those women who have performed great penance are fortunate enough to witness their lovers returning at this hour. The imagery of the returning herd and the maternal warmth of the cows belongs to the Mullai (pastoral) landscape, which symbolizes patient waiting and the hope of reunion. The key contrast lies between the fulfilled reunion of the animals and the painful separation of the human lovers.",
